=begin rakudoc

=TITLE Changelog

=SUBTITLE User-visible changes by release

=head1 Overview

This changelog follows the shape of Keep a Changelog, adapted to Rakudoc.
Versions use the C<META6.json> version number and release tags use the
C<release-x.y.z> convention.

=head1 Unreleased

=head2 Changed

=item Location::JSON tests call explicit C<.flush> after mutations (core
Tree no longer auto-flushes; plan §16.4.7 / §16.4.8). Conformance test
loads sibling C<Qwiratry::Test> via C<use lib>.

=item Default C<:path-transformer> with C<EMPTY> mold (plan §10.3 /
§16.4.3): ancestors become C<{}>, table-site / row-collection leaves
become C<[]>. Covered by C<t/03-location-json.rakutest>.

=item Default C<:transformer> is a C<Transformer> mold over
C<$*CONTEXT> rows (plan Q18 / §16.4.5). Callable overrides still work.

=item C<Qwiratry::DatabaseStorage::Location::JSON> now subclasses core
C<Qwiratry::DatabaseStorage::Location::Tree> and advertises today's
root/identity/object-key table shape as §8 Format projection defaults
(plus a default merge transformer). Omit-args C<useTable> behaviour is
unchanged; callers may override selectors / C<:transformer> for nested
tables.

=item Location::JSON tests and module examples cover omit-args defaults,
nested C<:row-selector> / C<:transformer> overrides that preserve
unselected document structure on flush, and clear
C<ProjectionUnresolved> errors for blank-Tree (XML-style) opens.

=head2 Added

=item C<Qwiratry::DatabaseStorage::Location::JSON> — Location-backed tables
using C<Format::JSON> (array-of-objects ↔ rows).

=head1 0.0.1 - 2026-07-04

=head2 Added

=item Initial release of the C<Qwiratry::Format::JSON> distribution, providing
C<Qwiratry::Format::JSON> as a real JSON parse/render backend for Qwiratry.

=item JSON parsing and rendering through L<JSON::Fast>.

=item Compact rendering by default, with support for C<:pretty>,
C<:spacing>, and C<:sorted-keys>.

=item Tests for explicit loading, format discovery, direct slang evaluation,
and autoload through installed C<provides> metadata.

=end rakudoc
